Fixes legacy defect L-17: passing a plain variable to a SUB whose parameters go to CALL ABSOLUTE (so they must live in conventional memory) read the variable id from a reference that has no sp3 separator, got id 0 and hit "subscript out of range" inside the compiler; because a successful $INCLUDE left qberrorhappened at -2/-3, the error handler then RESUMEd into the include loop and reported "File <statement> not found". Expected output is QBasic behaviour: the routine stores 1234 into the caller variable.
